<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">10 August in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">9 events that happened on 10 August, from 955 to 1945.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/otto-i" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/otto-i.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">955 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,071 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Otto I defeats the Magyars at the Battle of Lechfeld</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/augsburg">Augsburg</a>, King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/otto-i">Otto I</a>, outnumbered nearly two to one, began three days of fighting that ended in the defeat of the Hungarian army led by Bulcsú, Lél and Súr. The victory ended the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/magyars">Magyar</a> raids into the German lands.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-lechfeld">Battle of Lechfeld</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungarian-invasions-of-europe">Hungarian invasions of Europe</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/magyars">Magyars</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">991 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,035 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Vikings defeat Ealdorman Byrhtnoth at the Battle of Maldon</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Near Maldon, beside the River Blackwater in Essex, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vikings">Vikings</a> defeated the English under Byrhtnoth, ealdorman of Essex, who died in the battle. King Æthelred was then advised to buy the Vikings off, and they were paid 10,000 pounds to leave <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vikings">Vikings</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1030">1030 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">996 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Mirdasids of Aleppo rout Emperor Romanos III at Azaz</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Near the Syrian town of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/azaz">Azaz</a>, the forces of the Mirdasid emir of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aleppo">Aleppo</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shibl-al-dawla-nasr">Shibl al-Dawla Nasr</a>, defeated the much larger Byzantine army of Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romanos-iii-argyros">Romanos III Argyros</a>. The retreat became a rout in which Romanos barely escaped capture.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romanos-iii-argyros">Romanos III Argyros</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aleppo">Aleppo</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1628">1628 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">398 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Swedish warship Vasa sinks on her maiden voyage</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Top-heavy and unstable, the warship Vasa heeled over in a gust and sank in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stockholm">Stockholm</a> harbour less than a mile into her first voyage. Raised in 1961, she is now a celebrated museum ship.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1792">1792 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">234 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Insurgents storm the Tuileries Palace in Paris</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Armed Parisians and provincial volunteers attacked the Tuileries, killing hundreds of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/swiss-guards">Swiss Guards</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-xvi">Louis XVI</a> was suspended and imprisoned, and the French monarchy fell weeks later.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1793">1793 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">233 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Louvre opens as a public museum</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The revolutionary government opened the Muséum central des arts in the former royal palace, on the first anniversary of the monarchy's fall. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louvre">Louvre</a> became one of the world's greatest museums.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louvre">Louvre</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1809">1809 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">217 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Quito's patriots depose the Spanish authorities</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Criollo leaders in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/quito">Quito</a> overthrew the royal president and formed a governing junta, one of the first such moves in Spanish <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-america">South America</a>. It was crushed, but Ecuador won independence in 1822.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-america">South America</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1846">1846 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">180 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Congress establishes the Smithsonian Institution</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">President Polk signed the act creating the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/smithsonian">Smithsonian</a>, funded by the bequest of British chemist James Smithson. It grew into the world's largest museum, education and research complex.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/smithsonian">Smithsonian</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1945">1945 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">81 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Japan offers to surrender if the Emperor is preserved</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">After an imperial intervention, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> told the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/allies">Allies</a> it would accept the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/potsdam">Potsdam</a> terms provided the Emperor's prerogatives were kept. The US reply left his status to the Allied commander and the Japanese people.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/allies">Allies</a></div></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 10 August <span class="n">8</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/le-dai-hanh"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/le-dai-hanh.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Le Dai Hanh</span><span class="tp">941–1005</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/james-ii-of-aragon"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/james-ii-of-aragon.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">James II of Aragon</span><span class="tp">1267–1327</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/john-of-bohemia"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/john-of-bohemia.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">John of Bohemia</span><span class="tp">1296–1346</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/vicente-guerrero"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/vicente-guerrero.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Vicente Guerrero</span><span class="tp">1782–1831</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/camillo-benso-count-of-cavour"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/camillo-benso-count-of-cavour.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Camillo Benso, Count of Cavour</span><span class="tp">1810–1861</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/antanas-smetona"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/antanas-smetona.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Antanas Smetona</span><span class="tp">1874–1944</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/jorge-amado"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/jorge-amado.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Jorge Amado</span><span class="tp">1912–2001</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/anwar-ibrahim"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/anwar-ibrahim.jpg" alt="" loading